{"id": "clm:e7654bba4f4d71383c420457bf1e9754033eb99a2774a49bfc12d91dd87b0aa0", "type": "statement", "text": "For Atlas failures, test SRV resolution with dig SRV _mongodb._tcp.<cluster-host>, resolve each returned node hostname, then test TCP connectivity from the affected workload. Non-SRV URIs bypass SRV discovery but still contain hostnames requiring DNS. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/troubleshoot-connection.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:c010e6750b163b039e471db92a344c4ee6dafd26ad4fd56ec2ef42b172336136", "ev:cf1d2cacce30c9f32e4a2b834d21769b20d30c415617e17c33e171b9a3d84981"]}
{"id": "clm:db9cfeda75f05fe9a93e9db474c9268b555eb4d6859a1c20980cf30a6ce32dd4", "type": "statement", "text": "GKE enables NodeLocal DNSCache by default in Autopilot, where it cannot be disabled; Standard enables it by default starting at 1.34.1-gke.3720000. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-22)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/nodelocal-dns-cache", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e40cf148455e018fdef0ff06499d7a404fab8b5af2f08e3d86c6537d1ee92b14"]}
{"id": "clm:c9ad66b4776678732f926b44431c5d08d76330068f7244583a19862c74b91806", "type": "statement", "text": "Signicat’s December 2023 GKE report described CoreDNS NodeLocal forwarding to kube-dns over TCP, a hard-coded dnsmasq worker limit, and latency spikes coinciding with open connections above that limit. The author recommended Cloud DNS for that stack. This is a historical operational report, not an Atlas benchmark. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.signicat.com/blog/dont-use-nodelocal-dnscache-on-gke", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4ad9fa1934da0871d58bbe4f94b714d22c7a774108dfd1144b8ebb9feb864c93"]}
{"id": "clm:ac633caf0576fb13b93138bd9a873646091fb95ec13217e4849c33589e6cd7c4", "type": "statement", "text": "Signicat’s December 2023 report described a hard-coded 20-child dnsmasq limit in its GKE NodeLocal-to-kube-dns stack. Google’s GKE documentation distinguishes legacy kube-dns through version 1.35 from CoreDNS-based kube-dns in version 1.36 and later, so Signicat’s historical observation is not a universal current GKE limit. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-22)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/concepts/kube-dns", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.signicat.com/blog/dont-use-nodelocal-dnscache-on-gke"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:007d416c629e5a4d866acda199b457b71fcf6022c32d951baef996034f2981a9", "ev:229fc6d7507512803c758334df307b1283bf3167191a2cb825aa204a688f3f3c", "ev:4ad9fa1934da0871d58bbe4f94b714d22c7a774108dfd1144b8ebb9feb864c93"]}
{"id": "clm:57c78bd778b13d2ec83fee0fe7357e71f40596c5f8c778436b187f8dfb64f2a5", "type": "statement", "text": "NodeLocal DNSCache places a DNS cache on each GKE node, reducing central DNS load and lookup latency. It is a Kubernetes DNS optimization, not an Atlas feature. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/nodelocal-dns-cache", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://about.in.mercari.com/news/mercari-india/from-dns-failures-to-resilience-how-nodelocal-dnscache-saved-the-day-sanu-satyadarshi/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e40cf148455e018fdef0ff06499d7a404fab8b5af2f08e3d86c6537d1ee92b14"]}
{"id": "clm:3b64ab901a5b187a1400aec7d0c5c84842cb18eac77cacf130e173bb126b3e2d", "type": "statement", "text": "A July 25, 2025 community report describes intermittent UnknownHostException and server-selection timeouts from GKE Autopilot to peered Atlas despite successful connections. The report supplies no confirmed NodeLocal DNSCache diagnosis or remedy. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/gke-autopilot-atlas-vpc-peering-intermittent-dns-resolution-failures-despite-successful-java-driver-shell-connection/326252", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a3832c5f2e4479e457b1528bb72e9607b6ee078d422455acf11ffbf97ccd6a7e"]}
{"id": "clm:50e594cd8da4fe73a428704e43bb5ee748f878f1b69cc5aad937b443a2575fd9", "type": "statement", "text": "NodeLocal forwards external queries through the local metadata server, bypassing kube-dns. For its cache, positive records expire at the lesser of their TTL and 30 seconds; NXDOMAIN expires after five seconds. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-22)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/nodelocal-dns-cache", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0b5cbdd88f36408171c0ba107252783cb1e10e3aa6c2ab6dbc6ac91992d26852", "ev:685dca1596c815794bc002b049216b2a3555f7c3fdeacf7edf94388e92794cf3"]}
{"id": "clm:8ee1cdd6905f87de7cd82812156246fc92fcf50173708ce8730829f4e90e2d3d", "type": "statement", "text": "DNS egress policies can break NodeLocal resolution. Inspect the actual resolver path and permit its TCP/UDP DNS traffic; a namespace-only selector failed in Argo CD’s historical GKE incident. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/nodelocal-dns-cache", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/issues/11126"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ac87bb646738f6ff2e4444fc3a262be9798c601397110e98acdae7d2f246b483", "ev:cca145164b444292a6552ffcd040be83b47753ea9befad8004cb0712e105376e"]}
{"id": "clm:c344e47248c3e26048e30f8e5793bb4ba88019d015312eeda75e86a221f63973", "type": "statement", "text": "Mercari’s June 2025 engineering account reports a tenfold reduction in kube-dns calls and tenfold to hundredfold fewer DNS errors after NodeLocal rollout. These are workload-specific observations, not measured Atlas improvements. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-06-04)", "source_url": "https://about.in.mercari.com/news/mercari-india/from-dns-failures-to-resilience-how-nodelocal-dnscache-saved-the-day-sanu-satyadarshi/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5a427aeb68954f4eda5f19f54a81afe614c906ae830250b64856a2f1d181d0a4", "ev:5ac0ae25910c5280e98457c07773f826dfeefad543edc025eb3798746ea8959e", "ev:6375224a236693badf0e0ad95877474b466d7e59b943961fa05cb8fbe549c570"]}
{"id": "clm:998aa670485e36569aaec60ae6f3dad7bd36d02fd93596a2517335dd27fda3b9", "type": "statement", "text": "For kube-dns upstream timeout logs, Google suggests increasing kube-dns replicas; that workaround does not apply to metadata-server timeouts. Autopilot does not support the documented kube-dns-autoscaler customization. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-22)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/nodelocal-dns-cache", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["GKE NodeLocal DNSCache Atlas"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0bd2666ae59bedff6422a527cd3c51a92e8df99fc2d5c3a0ef4c03fbb701a59e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4df89bc9e5418a8d02361306746d8f710f8c4a72850e3c8ec10cdc40898886fc"]}
